; prior: Python — `if len(items):` as an emptiness test.
; expectation: len returns Int, which can never be falsy, so the then arm
; ALWAYS runs — even for an empty vector. E0209 fires and teaches the rule;
; the blessed spellings are [empty? v] or [> [len v] 0].
; principle: a latent prior mismatch becomes a taught rule (agent-first.md P2).
; expect-stdout: looks-nonempty
; expect-check: E0209
[fn main []
  [println [if [len #[]] "looks-nonempty" "empty"]]]
